.\" sngreprc(5) - sngrep configuration file
.TH SNGREPRC 5 "October 2026" "sngrep" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sngreprc \- configuration file for the sngrep SIP call-flow viewer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sngreprc
stores optional defaults for capture, SIP parsing, terminal displays,
filters, and the packet export dialog.
A configuration file may contain comments beginning with
.B #
and assignments of the form:
.PP
.RS
.nf
set setting.name value
.fi
.RE
.PP
The shipped example is
.BR /etc/sngreprc ,
or a copy of the source file
.BR config/sngreprc .
Settings are also available to inspect with
.BR "sngrep -D" .
Some settings depend on optional build features.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/sngreprc
System-wide defaults.
.TP
.B /usr/local/etc/sngreprc
Alternative system-wide location.
.TP
.B ~/.sngreprc
Per-user configuration.
.SH CAPTURE SETTINGS
.TP
.B capture.device
Capture device, a comma-separated device list, or
.BR any .
Example:
.B "set capture.device eth0"
.TP
.B capture.limit
Maximum stored call dialogs.
.TP
.B capture.buffer
Capture ring buffer size in megabytes.
.TP
.B capture.outfile
Default PCAP dump filename.
.TP
.B capture.rtp
Enable RTP capture; off by default.
.TP
.B capture.esp
Decode SIP within IPsec ESP with NULL encryption.
.TP
.B capture.rotate
Rotate the stored call list after the configured limit is reached.
.TP
.B capture.storage
Packet storage mode, for example
.BR memory .
.TP
.B capture.keyfile
RSA key file for optional TLS decryption (requires TLS support at build time).
.TP
.B capture.eep
Enable HEP/EEP decoding (requires HEP support at build time).
.SH SIP AND FILTER SETTINGS
.TP
.B sip.calls
Only list calls starting with INVITE.
.TP
.B sip.noincomplete
Ignore incomplete or response-only dialogs.
.TP
.B sip.xcid
Additional header names used to correlate dialogs, e.g.
.BR "X-Call-ID|X-CID" .
.TP
.B filter.methods
Comma-separated SIP methods to display.
.TP
.B filter.callstates
Call-state filter.
.TP
.B filter.payload
Payload filter expression.
.SH USER INTERFACE SETTINGS
.TP
.B background
Color background preference.
.TP
.B theme
Color theme:
.BR classic " (default), " modern ", " professional " or " simple .
Themes other than classic need a terminal with 256 colors and use the
terminal default background.
.TP
.B syntax
Enable or disable message syntax highlighting.
.TP
.B colormode
Call-flow color grouping mode.
.TP
.B mouse
Enable mouse support; on by default.
Set it to
.B off
to restore terminal text selection without holding Shift.
.TP
.B cl.scrollstep
Call List scrolling step.
.TP
.B cl.columnN
Configure the Nth visible Call List column; N starts at zero.
See the shipped example for supported fields.
.TP
.B cl.columnN.width
Width of the Nth Call List column.
.TP
.B cf.scrollstep
Call Flow scrolling step.
.TP
.B cf.rawminwidth
Minimum width for raw SIP message preview.
.TP
.B cf.rawfixedwidth
Fixed width for raw SIP message preview.
.TP
.B cf.highlight
Highlight mode for the selected Call Flow message.
.TP
.B savepath
Default path for the Save dialog.
.SH HEP/EEP SETTINGS
Available only when sngrep is built with HEP support.
.TP
.B eep.listen
Enable HEP listening.
.TP
.B eep.listen.address
Listener address.
.TP
.B eep.listen.port
Listener port (typically 9060).
.TP
.B eep.listen.proto
Listener transport,
.BR udp " (default) or " tcp .
TCP requires HEP version 3.
.TP
.B eep.listen.version
HEP protocol version.
.TP
.B eep.listen.pass
Optional HEP authentication secret.
.TP
.B eep.send
Enable HEP sending.
.TP
.B eep.send.address
HEP collector address.
.TP
.B eep.send.port
HEP collector port.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
# Capture SIP messages but not RTP.
set capture.device eth0
set capture.rtp off

# Save captures under a particular directory.
set savepath /var/tmp/sngrep

# Display selected columns.
set cl.column0 sipfrom
set cl.column1 sipto
set cl.column2 state
set cl.column2.width 14

# Only INVITE and REGISTER requests.
set filter.methods INVITE,REGISTER

# Use a 256 color theme and keep terminal text selection.
set theme modern
set mouse off

# Listen for HEP3 packets over TCP.
set eep.listen on
set eep.listen.proto tcp
set eep.listen.version 3
.fi
.RE
.SH NOTES
A BPF capture filter and a SIP display filter are different: a BPF
filter controls which frames libpcap passes to sngrep, while a SIP
display filter controls the call list.
In particular, port-only BPF filters may discard non-initial IP fragments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sngrep (8),
.BR pcap-filter (7)
